- In CPF cardAcceptor.name should be formatted like this:
	"SGBL*" + senderFirstName
	It also needs to be truncated to the max lenght of cardAcceptor.name 
	
- CPF: Always send in cardAcceptor.address: these: addressLine, state, zipCode

- CPF always send senderMiddleName + recipientMiddleName 
	
- "merchantCategoryCode": "6012" should also be always sent in CPF

- CPF: We should always send : "cardAcceptor.legalBusinessName" : "SGBL"
	
- If Cross-Border OCT to  Australia or Canada --> recipientAddressLine1=Must be Present
recipientCity=Must be Present
recipientState=Must be Present
recipientPostalCode=Must be Present
recipientCountryCode=Must be Present
senderPostalCode=Must be Present
senderStateCode=Must be Present

- If Cross-Border OCT to South Africa: we need to send the recipientMiddleName +     "senderMiddleName"

If the card is indian, we need to send the purposeOfPayment, sourceAmount and sourceCurrencyCode (note hat purposeOfPayment need to have certain specific values that can be found in this file Visa Direct for Card (AFT & OCT) Processing Guide
 
Appendix E – Purpose of Payment Standardized Codes List) WE CAN STICK TO THIS purposeOfPayment: ISMP2P or ISOTHR


